{
  "format": "TaleWeaver",
  "version": "1.3.1",
  "adventure": {
    "origin_id": "20e23627-93ab-46a3-b93d-7fde43a15f62",
    "title": "Suburban Sabotage",
    "teaser": "Two hours until Grandma's inspection! Fix the sink, glue the Ming dish, and uncover a wild family plot.",
    "cover_appearance": "chaotic suburban kitchen, flooded sink, broken Ming vase, cartoon 90s adventure style, vibrant",
    "version": "1.1.1",
    "creator": "Jean Schmitz",
    "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 by Jean Schmitz",
    "license": "CC BY-NC 4.0",
    "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/",
    "language": null,
    "original_prompt": "Premise: It is 16:00 on a chaotic Saturday afternoon at the Miller family home. At 18:00 sharp (after 2 hours of in-game time), Dad's wealthy, tyrannical mother @GRANDMA arrives for dinner inspection. If the house is not spotless and the casserole is not baking inside Grandma's sacred Ming porcelain dish, she will evict the Millers and ship @GRANDPA_JOE off to the cheap Shady Pines nursing home. Ten-year-old Jack is left to fix the flooded kitchen sink, glue Mom's shattered heirloom dish back together, bake the casserole, and get rid of freeloading neighbor @KEVIN using Dad's fiercely guarded \"Sports Magazines\". Tone: fast-paced 90s LucasArts comedy full of witty double entendres filtered through an innocent kid's eyes.\nAntagonist: @GRANDMA (the impending 18:00 deadline who secretly plans to sell the family house to fund a yacht for her 24-year-old poolboy Raul) and @KEVIN (the clingy neighbor who stalks Jack from 16:30 onwards, wastes precious time, and blocks the kitchen oven).\nTwist: In Sequence 4, when @DAD unscrews the clogged sink pipe with his @GOLDEN_WRENCH, he pulls out a mini hacksaw and @BOX_KEY. @GRANDPA_JOE intentionally sabotaged the Ming dish and clogged the sink before throwing his back out! Unlocking @GRANDPAS_BOX under the bed in @GRANDPAS_ROOM reveals @POOLBOY_PHOTOS and @GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX: Grandma already plans to evict the family tonight no matter what, to run away with her poolboy Raul! To stop her, Jack must combine the @PRENUP_CONTRACT from @MOMS_OFFICE with @POOLBOY_PHOTOS into the @BLACKMAIL_DOSSIER, proving that under Paragraph 7 (Morality Clause), Grandma loses her entire fortune to Grandpa Joe if her affair is exposed.\nTwist clues: (1) Sequence 1: @PRENUP_CONTRACT in @MOMS_OFFICE details Paragraph 7 (the strict Morality Clause regarding household and pool staff) with a note that Grandpa asked for it yesterday, while @BROKEN_DISH shows clean saw marks on the handle; (2) Sequence 2: @DETECTIVE_BILL in @GRANDPAS_ROOM shows Grandpa hired \"Discrete Poolside Investigations\" to spy on Grandma's villa.\nEngine features used: time triggers (on_time_reached at 30m, 1h, 1h45m, and 2h with 3-minute ticks), choice dialogs, constructable recipes, switches, container locks, item handovers, NPC hiding - requires Event Scripts ON.\nDesign rule: no counting puzzles, no plain-text or simply split codes, every puzzle has a fair clue trail.\n\n[World]\nlanguage: en\nwin: Before 18:00, the kitchen sink is repaired, Kevin is gone, the spiced casserole is baking in the glued Ming dish, and the Blackmail Dossier is ready for Grandma.\nlose: The clock reaches 18:00 before all preparations and the blackmail trap are complete, or Jack loses the game.\nwin_guard: tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False) and tw.flags.get('CASSEROLE_DONE') and tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and tw.vars.get('grandma_trapped', False)\nlose_guard: tw.vars.get('grandma_failed', False)\ninit_script: |\n  tw.time.set_minutes_per_tick(3)\n  tw.time.allow_gm_time(False)\n  tw.vars.set('kevin_active', False)\n  tw.vars.set('kevin_gone', False)\n  tw.vars.set('sink_fixed', False)\n  tw.vars.set('casserole_baked', False)\n  tw.vars.set('grandma_trapped', False)\n  tw.vars.set('buster_gone', False)\n  def check_victory():\n      if tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False) and tw.flags.get('CASSEROLE_DONE') and tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and tw.vars.get('grandma_trapped', False):\n          tw.game.win('Perfect timing! Before 18:00 strikes, the sink shines, Kevin is home studying \"floor gymnastics\", the casserole bakes in the glued Ming dish, and the Poolboy Blackmail Dossier lies ready on the table. When Grandma walks in and sees Paragraph 7 clipped to photos of her and Poolboy Raul, she turns pale, tears up the eviction notice, signs the house over to Dad, and flees!')\n  def lure_cat_action():\n      if tw.vars.get('buster_gone', False):\n          return\n      tw.vars.set('buster_gone', True)\n      tw.player.remove_item('CAT_TREATS')\n      tw.npcs.move('CAT_WHISKERS', 'BACKYARD')\n      tw.npcs.hide('CAT_WHISKERS')\n      tw.npcs.hide('DOG_BUSTER')\n      tw.objects.reveal('MEATY_BONE')\n      tw.story.narrate('Drawn by the irresistible scent of crunchy catnip, Mr. Whiskers bolts into the backyard! Buster the bulldog loses his mind, abandons his meaty bone, and chases the cat barking wildly through the garden hedge!')\n  def on_tina_dialog(answ):\n      if answ == 0:\n          tw.player.damage(2)\n          tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'Get out of my room, you little dork!')\n          tw.story.narrate('Tina hurls a heavy decorative pillow right at your face (-2 HP).')\n          return\n      if answ == 1:\n          tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'Nice try! Mom locked herself in her office until five.')\n          return\n      if answ == 2:\n          tw.player.remove_item('FIZZY_DRINK')\n          tw.vars.set('tina_bribed', True)\n          tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'OMG, Pink Glitter Zero! Step back and watch a master of teenage drama at work... MOOOOM! HELP! MY HAIR STRAIGHTENER EXPLODED AND MY EYEBROWS ARE GONE!')\n          tw.npcs.move('MOM', 'TINAS_ROOM')\n          tw.exits.unlock('KITCHEN', 'MOMS_OFFICE')\n          tw.objects.reveal('TINAS_DIARY')\n          tw.story.narrate('Tina lets out an ear-splitting scream right here in her room! Seconds later, Mom unlocks her office door downstairs and sprints up into Tina\\'s room in total panic. As Tina leaps onto her bed for dramatic effect, her secret diary slips out from under her pillow!')\n\n[Protagonist] Jack Miller\nrole: Ten-year-old youngest son and reluctant family crisis manager\ngoal: Fix the sink, glue the Ming dish and bake the casserole, get rid of Kevin, and uncover Grandpa's secret plan before Grandma arrives at 18:00.\nhp: 30\n\n[Script: TIMELINE_1600_INTRO] 16:00 Chaos Start\ntrigger: on_init\ncode: |\n  tw.story.narrate('It is 16:00 sharp! In exactly two hours, tyrannical Grandma arrives for dinner inspection. Mom locks herself inside her home office in tears. Tina slams her bedroom door upstairs. Dad is kneeling under the flooded kitchen sink, cursing because he cannot find his golden wrench, while Grandpa Joe grumbles in front of the dead TV. Everything is up to you, Jack!')\n\n[Script: TIMELINE_1630_KEVIN] 16:30 Kevin Appears\ntrigger: on_time_reached\nat: 30m\ncode: |\n  if not tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and not tw.vars.get('kevin_active', False):\n      tw.vars.set('kevin_active', True)\n      tw.npcs.reveal('KEVIN')\n      tw.npcs.move_to_player('KEVIN')\n      tw.npcs.say('KEVIN', 'Hey Jack! Do I smell dinner? Got five bucks or something to eat?')\n      tw.story.narrate('16:30 sharp: Annoying neighbor Kevin suddenly stands right next to you, uninvited!')\n\n[Script: TIMELINE_1700_WARNING] 17:00 One Hour Left\ntrigger: on_time_reached\nat: 1h\ncode: |\n  tw.story.narrate('The wall clock chimes 17:00! Only one hour left until Grandma arrives, and Dad is still sweating buckets under the sink!')\n\n[Script: TIMELINE_1745_PANIC] 17:45 Fifteen Minutes Left\ntrigger: on_time_reached\nat: 1h45m\ncode: |\n  tw.story.narrate('It is 17:45! Grandma\\'s taxi just turned onto your street! Fifteen minutes left, hurry up!')\n\n[Script: KEVIN_STALKER] Kevin Randomly Stalks Jack and Wastes Time\ntrigger: on_enter_scene\ncode: |\n  if tw.vars.get('kevin_active', False) and not tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False):\n      if tw.dice.d6() >= 3:\n          tw.npcs.move_to_player('KEVIN')\n          tw.time.advance(3)\n          tw.npcs.say_directed('KEVIN', 'pesters Jack with pointless questions about food, pocket money, or video games, wasting 3 precious minutes')\n\n[Script: TIMELINE_1800_GRANDMA] 18:00 Grandma Arrives in the Kitchen\ntrigger: on_time_reached\nat: 2h\ncode: |\n  tw.npcs.reveal('GRANDMA')\n  tw.npcs.move('GRANDMA', 'KITCHEN')\n  if tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False) and tw.flags.get('CASSEROLE_DONE') and tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and tw.vars.get('grandma_trapped', False):\n      tw.npcs.say('GRANDMA', 'Well, the sink is clean and my Ming dish is in the oven... WAIT A SECOND! Where did you get those photos of Raul and me?! Is that Paragraph 7 of my Marriage Contract?! Fine! Keep the house, and Joe can stay here forever!')\n      tw.game.win('18:00 sharp: Grandma is completely checkmated by the spotless kitchen AND the Poolboy Blackmail Dossier!')\n  else:\n      tw.vars.set('grandma_failed', True)\n      tw.npcs.say('GRANDMA', 'Just as I expected! An absolute pigsty, and no leverage to stop me! Pack your bags, Millers, I am selling this house and shipping Joe to Shady Pines tonight!')\n      tw.game.game_over('18:00 sharp: Grandma stands in the kitchen with the eviction papers. You are grounded until 2035!')\n\n[Sidequest: SQ_PEACE_AND_QUIET] Peace and Quiet\ngoal: Permanently get rid of annoying neighbor Kevin using Dad's \"Sports Magazines\".\nguard: tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False)\nxp: 50\n\n[Award: MASTER_CHEF] Flawless Crisis Manager\ntier: gold\nrequires: Complete all tasks and trap Grandma before 18:00 without losing a single HP to Tina, the piranhas, or Buster the dog.\nguard: tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False) and tw.flags.get('CASSEROLE_DONE') and tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and tw.vars.get('grandma_trapped', False) and tw.player.hp >= 30\n\n[Sequence: 1] Operation Distraction\nJack starts in the @KITCHEN at 16:00. @MOM locked herself inside @MOMS_OFFICE and @TINA is sulking upstairs in @TINAS_ROOM. Jack opens the @FRIDGE and takes the @FIZZY_DRINK (and can also take the @FROZEN_CASSEROLE). Talking to @TINA in @TINAS_ROOM opens a Choice Dialog where Jack bribes her with @FIZZY_DRINK. Right there in @TINAS_ROOM, Tina screams at the top of her lungs about an eyebrow emergency, making @MOM unlock @MOMS_OFFICE and rush upstairs into @TINAS_ROOM while revealing @TINAS_DIARY under Tina's pillow. Reading @TINAS_DIARY and checking the @FIRE_CERTIFICATE in the @LIVING_ROOM (year 2019 backwards = 9102) gives the code 9102 to unlock @MOMS_DESK in @MOMS_OFFICE, yielding the @BATTERIES and @CAT_TREATS. In @MOMS_OFFICE, Jack also picks up the @BROKEN_DISH (Grandma's shattered Ming casserole dish) and the @PRENUP_CONTRACT.\nChoice Dialog: Talking to @TINA in @TINAS_ROOM - options: \"Help me clean up, Grandma is coming!\" (-2 HP), \"Mom said you have to come downstairs right now!\" (Tina laughs it off), \"Here is your Pink Glitter Drink if you lure Mom out of her office!\" (only if Jack has FIZZY_DRINK: Tina screams in her room, Mom rushes into TINAS_ROOM, unlocks MOMS_OFFICE and reveals TINAS_DIARY).\ngoal_item: BATTERIES\nend: Jack lures Mom out of her office, collects the broken Ming dish and marriage contract, and unlocks Mom's desk drawer to get the fresh AA batteries.\n\n[Scene: KITCHEN] Kitchen\nThe chaotic center of the Miller house. Dirty dishes are piled up, and murky water drips steadily from the clogged sink pipe.\n\n[Scene: LIVING_ROOM] Living Room\nA cozy but messy living room with a deep sofa, a huge dark television, and a framed certificate on the wall.\n\n[Scene: TINAS_ROOM] Tina's Room\nBoyband posters on the walls, loud pop music, and a strict \"NO LITTLE BROTHERS ALLOWED\" sign on the door.\n\n[Scene: MOMS_OFFICE] Mom's Office\nA usually neat home office filled with legal binders, tissues, and a heavy oak desk.\n\n[Scene: BACKYARD] Backyard\nA small fenced garden behind the house featuring a large wooden doghouse near the hedge.\n\n[Exit: KITCHEN <-> LIVING_ROOM] the hallway arch\n[Exit: LIVING_ROOM <-> TINAS_ROOM] the stairs to Tina's room\n[Exit: KITCHEN <-> BACKYARD] the patio sliding door\n\n[Exit: KITCHEN <-> MOMS_OFFICE] the door to Mom's office\nguard: tw.vars.get('tina_bribed', False)\nlock: Mom locked the door from the inside while sobbing on the phone. Only a full-blown teenage emergency upstairs will make her come out.\n\n[NPC: DAD] Dad\nin: KITCHEN\nkillable: no\non_interact: |\n  if tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False):\n      tw.npcs.say('DAD', \"The sink is finally draining! Now figure out why your Grandpa's key and a mini hacksaw were jammed inside our drainpipe!\")\n  elif not tw.vars.get('dad_locker_hint_given', False):\n      tw.vars.set('dad_locker_hint_given', True)\n      tw.npcs.say('DAD', 'Jack, I need my golden wrench from the Mancave! And whatever you do, stay away from my locker down there! Mom thinks the code is our anniversary, hah! Nope. It is the numbers I admire most on my Miss Fitness July poster... well, only the upper half of them. Do not tell your mother!')\n  else:\n      tw.npcs.say('DAD', 'Golden wrench, Jack! Mancave! And keep your sticky fingers off my locker, you hear me?')\non_receive_item: |\n  if 'GOLDEN_WRENCH' in received_item_ids:\n      tw.vars.set('sink_fixed', True)\n      tw.objects.reveal('BOX_KEY')\n      tw.objects.move_item('BOX_KEY', 'player')\n      tw.npcs.say('DAD', 'My golden wrench! Let me unscrew this U-bend... Wait a second! Why was there a mini hacksaw and a small brass key with a waterproof tag jammed inside our sink pipe?! Take this key, Jack!')\n      check_victory()\n  elif 'SPORTS_MAGAZINES' in received_item_ids:\n      tw.npcs.give_to_player('DAD', 'SPORTS_MAGAZINES')\n      tw.npcs.say('DAD', 'ARE YOU OUT OF YOUR MIND, SON?! Hide those immediately! Uh... I mean, those are highly advanced orthopedic journals about beach calisthenics! If your mother or Grandma sees my \"Sports Magazines\", I am a dead man!')\n  else:\n      for item_id in received_item_ids:\n          tw.npcs.give_to_player('DAD', item_id)\n      tw.npcs.say('DAD', 'That won\\'t loosen this rusted pipe, buddy! I need my golden wrench!')\nA slightly chubby, sweating man who is terrified of his mother Grandma and desperately trying to fix the kitchen sink.\n\n[NPC: MOM] Mom\nin: MOMS_OFFICE\nkillable: no\non_receive_item: |\n  for item_id in received_item_ids:\n      tw.npcs.give_to_player('MOM', item_id)\n  if 'SPORTS_MAGAZINES' in received_item_ids:\n      tw.npcs.say('MOM', 'Not now, Jack! Put your father\\'s weird gymnastics brochures away before Grandma gets here!')\n  elif 'BROKEN_DISH' in received_item_ids:\n      tw.npcs.say('MOM', 'Oh God, hide it! I barely touched Grandma\\'s sacred Ming casserole dish and it snapped right in half! Unless you find industrial super glue and bake the casserole inside it, we are doomed!')\n  else:\n      tw.npcs.say('MOM', 'Sweetheart, please, Mommy is having a nervous breakdown right now!')\nA stressed businesswoman wearing a Bluetooth headset and dabbing her eyes with tissues.\n\n[NPC: TINA] Tina\nin: TINAS_ROOM\nkillable: no\non_interact: |\n  if not tw.vars.get('tina_bribed', False):\n      tw.dialog.choose(\n          'Tina glares at you annoyed: \"What are you doing in my room, squirt?!\"',\n          [\n              'Help me clean up, Grandma is coming!',\n              'Mom said you have to come downstairs right now!',\n              {'label': 'Here is your Pink Glitter Drink if you scream and lure Mom out of her office!', 'visible_if': \"tw.player.has_item('FIZZY_DRINK')\"}\n          ],\n          on_choice='on_tina_dialog',\n          speaker='Tina'\n      )\n  else:\n      tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'Leave me alone, I am busy convincing Mom that I need emergency spa money!')\non_receive_item: |\n  for item_id in received_item_ids:\n      tw.npcs.give_to_player('TINA', item_id)\n  if 'SPORTS_MAGAZINES' in received_item_ids:\n      tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'Ewww, gross! Get Dad\\'s creepy \"Sports Magazines\" away from me, you little weirdo!')\n  else:\n      tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'Talk to me properly if you want to make a deal, dork!')\nJack's older sister in the peak of puberty, thoroughly annoyed by her little brother.\n\n[NPC: GRANDPA_JOE] Grandpa Joe\nin: LIVING_ROOM\ninventory: MANCAVE_KEY\nkillable: no\non_receive_item: |\n  if 'WORKING_REMOTE' in received_item_ids:\n      tw.npcs.give_to_player('GRANDPA_JOE', 'MANCAVE_KEY')\n      tw.npcs.say('GRANDPA_JOE', 'Finally the TV works! Here, take the spare key to your Dad\\'s secret Mancave. Oh, and Jack... if my cursed back hadn\\'t given out in the kitchen earlier, I would have ruined your Grandma\\'s scheming tonight! Just don\\'t look under my bed!')\n  elif 'BLACKMAIL_DOSSIER' in received_item_ids:\n      tw.vars.set('grandma_trapped', True)\n      tw.npcs.say('GRANDPA_JOE', 'Bwahaha! Paragraph 7 of our Marriage Contract paperclipped right onto the glossy photos of Grandma and Poolboy Raul! I will lay this right on the kitchen table for her 18:00 inspection. She is toast, my boy!')\n      check_victory()\n  elif 'POOLBOY_PHOTOS' in received_item_ids or 'PRENUP_CONTRACT' in received_item_ids:\n      for item_id in received_item_ids:\n          tw.npcs.give_to_player('GRANDPA_JOE', item_id)\n      tw.npcs.say('GRANDPA_JOE', 'Close, my boy! But we need the complete trap: combine the Poolboy Photos with the Marriage Contract from your Mom\\'s office into one watertight Blackmail Dossier!')\n  elif 'SPORTS_MAGAZINES' in received_item_ids:\n      tw.npcs.give_to_player('GRANDPA_JOE', 'SPORTS_MAGAZINES')\n      tw.npcs.say('GRANDPA_JOE', 'Haha, the October \\'98 Beach Aerobics issue! Tell your father the blonde on page 4 has definitely never held a volleyball in her life. Keep them away before my pacemaker acts up!')\n  else:\n      for item_id in received_item_ids:\n          tw.npcs.give_to_player('GRANDPA_JOE', item_id)\n      tw.npcs.say('GRANDPA_JOE', 'What am I supposed to do with that? Bring me my TV remote WITH working batteries!')\nSits stiffly in his armchair in front of the dark television, rubbing his lower back and grumbling about his ex-wife Grandma.\n\n[NPC: KEVIN] Kevin\nin: KITCHEN\nhidden: yes\nreveal: script\nkillable: no\non_receive_item: |\n  if 'SPORTS_MAGAZINES' in received_item_ids:\n      tw.vars.set('kevin_gone', True)\n      tw.vars.set('kevin_active', False)\n      tw.npcs.say('KEVIN', 'WHOA! Dude! Are those your Dad\\'s legendary \"Sports Magazines\" in the uncensored glossy edition?! Uh... I gotta go home right now! I need to... study for gym class tomorrow! See ya next week, Jack!')\n      tw.npcs.hide('KEVIN')\n      check_victory()\n  else:\n      for item_id in received_item_ids:\n          tw.npcs.give_to_player('KEVIN', item_id)\n      tw.npcs.say('KEVIN', 'Booooring! Don\\'t you have anything cooler or something to eat?')\nThe super clingy neighbor boy who shows up uninvited at 16:30 and wastes Jack's time.\n\n[NPC: GRANDMA] Grandma\nin: KITCHEN\nhidden: yes\nreveal: script\nkillable: no\nDad's wealthy, domineering mother, arriving at 18:00 sharp with white inspection gloves and eviction papers.\n\n[Container: FRIDGE] Refrigerator\nin: KITCHEN\nportable: no\ncontains: FROZEN_CASSEROLE, FIZZY_DRINK\nA packed family fridge humming loudly in the corner of the kitchen.\n\n[Item: FIZZY_DRINK] Pink Glitter Energy Drink\ntype: PICKABLE\nTina's sacred, ice-cold favorite beverage.\n\n[Item: FROZEN_CASSEROLE] Frozen Casserole Block\ntype: PICKABLE\nA rock-hard block of frozen unseasoned casserole from the freezer, taken out of its plastic tub.\n\n[Readable: TINAS_DIARY] Tina's Diary\nin: TINAS_ROOM\nhidden: yes\nreveal: script\ntext: Dear Diary, Mom really thinks her desk drawer code is uncrackable. It is literally just the year on Dad's embarrassing Fire Department Certificate in the living room spelled backwards! Also, why was Grandpa sneaking out of Mom's office with a mini hacksaw today?\n\n[Readable: FIRE_CERTIFICATE] Fire Department Certificate\nin: LIVING_ROOM\nportable: no\ntext: Official Certificate of the Volunteer Fire Brigade: Presenting the Miller Family with an official warning for the Most Spectacular Barbecue Disaster of the Year 2019.\n\n[Item: BROKEN_DISH] Shattered Ming Casserole Dish\nin: MOMS_OFFICE\ntype: PICKABLE\nGrandma's sacred porcelain casserole dish, broken cleanly into two halves. Strange: there are tiny saw marks right on the ceramic handle!\n\n[Readable: PRENUP_CONTRACT] Grandparents' Marriage Contract\nin: MOMS_OFFICE\nportable: yes\ntext: MILLER FAMILY TRUST & PRENUPTIAL AGREEMENT. Paragraph 7 (The Ironclad Morality Clause): Should either spouse be caught engaging in improper poolside wrestling with household or pool staff, 100% of the fortune, the villa, and the Miller family home immediately transfer to the innocent spouse. (Sticky note from Mom: Grandpa asked me to copy this page yesterday!)\n\n[Container: MOMS_DESK] Locked Desk Drawer\nin: MOMS_OFFICE\nportable: no\ncode: 9102\ncontains: BATTERIES, CAT_TREATS\nMom's heavily secured desk drawer where she locks away confiscated household items.\n\n[Item: BATTERIES] Pair of AA Batteries\ntype: PICKABLE\nTwo fresh batteries confiscated by Mom so Grandpa wouldn't blast the TV at full volume.\n\n[Item: CAT_TREATS] Crunchy Catnip Treats\ntype: PICKABLE\non_use: |\n  if tw.scene.id == 'BACKYARD':\n      lure_cat_action()\n  else:\n      tw.story.narrate('Mr. Whiskers perks his ears up! Better scatter these treats out in the Backyard right in front of Buster the dog!')\nIrresistible snacks for lazy house cats.\n\n[Sequence: 2] Key to the Mancave & Dad's Secret Stash\nIn the @LIVING_ROOM, Jack searches the @COUCH to find the @EMPTY_REMOTE. Using @RECIPE_REMOTE, Jack combines @EMPTY_REMOTE and @BATTERIES into @WORKING_REMOTE. Giving @WORKING_REMOTE to @GRANDPA_JOE makes him hand over the @MANCAVE_KEY and drop a suspicious remark about his bed in @GRANDPAS_ROOM. In @GRANDPAS_ROOM, Jack spots the locked @GRANDPAS_BOX under the bed and reads the @DETECTIVE_BILL. Unlocking the @SECRET_MANCAVE with @MANCAVE_KEY lets Jack inspect the @FITNESS_POSTER (stats 90 - 60 - 90). Combining Dad's hint (\"the numbers I admire most on my Miss Fitness July poster... only the upper half of them\") with @FITNESS_POSTER gives code 9060 to open @DADS_LOCKER, yielding @SPORTS_MAGAZINES (to get rid of @KEVIN anytime) and @SUPER_GLUE (to glue @BROKEN_DISH into @MING_DISH via @RECIPE_GLUE_DISH).\ngoal_item: MANCAVE_KEY\nend: Grandpa Joe turns on the television and slips Jack the key to Dad's Secret Mancave.\n\n[Scene: GRANDPAS_ROOM] Grandpa's Room\nA ground-floor guest room smelling of peppermint and old cigars. A heavy wooden chest sits pushed deep under the bed.\n\n[Scene: SECRET_MANCAVE] Secret Mancave\nDad's secret sanctuary behind a heavy steel door: neon signs, a poker table, a locked steel locker, and a bubbling piranha aquarium.\n\n[Exit: LIVING_ROOM <-> GRANDPAS_ROOM] the ground-floor guest room door\n\n[Exit: LIVING_ROOM <-> SECRET_MANCAVE] the hidden steel door behind the bookshelf\nkey_item: MANCAVE_KEY\n\n[Container: COUCH] Living Room Couch\nin: LIVING_ROOM\nportable: no\ncontains: EMPTY_REMOTE\nThings constantly vanish between these deep sofa cushions.\n\n[Item: EMPTY_REMOTE] Empty TV Remote\ntype: PICKABLE\nGrandpa's beloved remote control. The battery compartment is completely empty.\n\n[Recipe: RECIPE_REMOTE] Insert Batteries into Remote\ncombine: EMPTY_REMOTE + BATTERIES\nresults: WORKING_REMOTE\n\n[Item: WORKING_REMOTE] Working TV Remote\ntype: PICKABLE\nThe remote control loaded with fresh batteries.\n\n[Item: MANCAVE_KEY] Heavy Steel Door Key\ntype: KEY\nOpens the steel door to Dad's Secret Mancave.\n\n[Readable: DETECTIVE_BILL] Private Detective Invoice\nin: GRANDPAS_ROOM\nportable: no\ntext: INVOICE - Discrete Poolside Investigations Ltd. Client: Joe Miller. Subject: Surveillance of Grandma Evelyn's Villa Jacuzzi & 24-year-old \"Aqua-Aerobics Coach\" Raul. Status: High-resolution photographic proof delivered!\n\n[Container: GRANDPAS_BOX] Locked Chest Under the Bed\nin: GRANDPAS_ROOM\nportable: no\nunlock_item: BOX_KEY\ncontains: POOLBOY_PHOTOS, GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX\nGrandpa Joe's padlocked iron cigar chest hidden under his bed frame.\n\n[Readable: FITNESS_POSTER] \"Miss Fitness July\" Poster\nin: SECRET_MANCAVE\nportable: no\ntext: A glossy poster titled \"Championship Beach Stretching '98\". The athlete forgot her uniform too. At the bottom it reads: \"Official Athletic Record Stats: 90 - 60 - 90\".\n\n[Container: DADS_LOCKER] Dad's \"Strictly Athletics\" Locker\nin: SECRET_MANCAVE\nportable: no\ncode: 9060\ncontains: SPORTS_MAGAZINES, SUPER_GLUE\nA heavy steel locker labeled \"Boring Tax Returns & Orthopaedic Sports Almanacs - Keep Out!\".\n\n[Readable: SPORTS_MAGAZINES] Bundle of \"Sports Magazines\"\ntype: READABLE\nportable: yes\ntext: The cover says \"EXTREME FLOOR GYMNASTICS - Special Edition\". Weird: all the female athletes completely forgot to wear their team jerseys, even though it looks super windy on that beach. Also, pages 14 to 18 are stuck together. Dad must have spilled his protein shake while studying their stretching routines.\non_read: |\n  tw.story.narrate('You flip through Dad\\'s \"Sports Magazines\" in confusion. Not a single football score table in here! Just remarkably flexible ladies who seem to have lost their contact lenses on a bearskin rug.')\nDad's fiercely guarded collection of glossy \"Sports Magazines\". Jack is 100% convinced they are about competitive calisthenics.\n\n[Item: SUPER_GLUE] Industrial Super Glue\ntype: PICKABLE\nDad's ultra-strong epoxy adhesive. Bonds porcelain in three seconds flat.\n\n[Recipe: RECIPE_GLUE_DISH] Glue the Shattered Ming Dish\ncombine: BROKEN_DISH + SUPER_GLUE\nresults: MING_DISH\n\n[Item: MING_DISH] Glued Ming Casserole Dish\ntype: PICKABLE\nGrandma's prized porcelain baking dish, seamlessly glued back together. So long as nobody taps it too hard, it looks brand new!\n\n[Sequence: 3] Dog, Cat, Piranha!\nIn the @SECRET_MANCAVE, Jack sees the @GOLDEN_WRENCH at the bottom of the @PIRANHA_TANK. To get the @MEATY_BONE guarded by @DOG_BUSTER in the @BACKYARD, Jack goes to the @BACKYARD with the @CAT_TREATS and uses them (or triggers @LURE_CAT_TO_YARD) to lure @CAT_WHISKERS outside. @DOG_BUSTER chases @CAT_WHISKERS out of the yard and leaves the @MEATY_BONE behind. Putting the @MEATY_BONE into the @PIRANHA_TANK distracts the piranhas and hands Jack the @GOLDEN_WRENCH.\ngoal_item: GOLDEN_WRENCH\nend: The piranhas are busy gnawing on the bone and Jack retrieves Dad's golden wrench from the tank.\n  [Rule: LURE_CAT_TO_YARD] Jack uses or scatters the Crunchy Catnip Treats in the backyard to lure Mr. Whiskers in front of Buster the dog.\n  guard: tw.scene.id == 'BACKYARD' and tw.player.has_item('CAT_TREATS') and not tw.vars.get('buster_gone', False)\n  script: lure_cat_action()\n  max: 1\n\n[NPC: DOG_BUSTER] Buster the Dog\nin: BACKYARD\ntype: ANIMAL\nkillable: no\non_interact: |\n  tw.player.damage(5)\n  tw.story.narrate('Buster growls menacingly in front of his doghouse and snaps at your hand (-5 HP)! Unless he is distracted by his arch-nemesis the cat, you will never get that bone.')\non_receive_item: |\n  for item_id in received_item_ids:\n      tw.npcs.give_to_player('DOG_BUSTER', item_id)\n  tw.story.narrate('Buster ignores your offering and guards his meaty bone fiercely. Only chasing a cat in the backyard would make him abandon his post!')\nA stubborn family bulldog guarding a juicy bone in front of his doghouse.\n\n[NPC: CAT_WHISKERS] Mr. Whiskers the Cat\nin: LIVING_ROOM\ntype: ANIMAL\nkillable: no\non_receive_item: |\n  for item_id in received_item_ids:\n      tw.npcs.give_to_player('CAT_WHISKERS', item_id)\n  if 'CAT_TREATS' in received_item_ids:\n      tw.story.narrate('Mr. Whiskers purrs greedily and eyes the bag of treats. If you use or scatter the catnip treats out in the backyard, he will sprint right past Buster\\'s doghouse!')\n  else:\n      tw.story.narrate('Mr. Whiskers yawns arrogantly and ignores it.')\nThe lazy house cat who would sprint through fire for crunchy catnip.\n\n[Item: MEATY_BONE] Half-Gnawed Meaty Bone\nin: BACKYARD\nhidden: yes\nreveal: script\ntype: PICKABLE\nA large bone still covered in juicy meat scraps, left behind by Buster.\n\n[Container: PIRANHA_TANK] Piranha Aquarium\nin: SECRET_MANCAVE\nportable: no\non_interact: |\n  if not tw.vars.get('piranhas_fed', False):\n      tw.player.damage(8)\n      tw.story.narrate('You dip your fingers toward the water and SNAP! A ravenous piranha bites you (-8 HP). You need to put something meaty inside (Put In) to distract them!')\non_items_added: |\n  if 'MEATY_BONE' in added_item_ids:\n      tw.vars.set('piranhas_fed', True)\n      tw.objects.destroy('MEATY_BONE')\n      tw.objects.reveal('GOLDEN_WRENCH')\n      tw.objects.move_item('GOLDEN_WRENCH', 'player')\n      tw.story.narrate('The piranhas go into a feeding frenzy over the meaty bone! You quickly reach to the bottom of the tank and pull out Dad\\'s golden wrench!')\n  else:\n      for item_id in added_item_ids:\n          tw.objects.take_from_container('PIRANHA_TANK', item_id, to='player')\n      tw.story.narrate('The piranhas ignore that completely. They want real meat on a bone!')\nAt the bottom of the tank, Dad's golden wrench glitters among hungry carnivorous fish.\n\n[Item: GOLDEN_WRENCH] Golden Wrench\nin: SECRET_MANCAVE\nhidden: yes\nreveal: script\ntype: TOOL\nDad's prized plumbing tool.\n\n[Sequence: 4] The Truth in the Drainpipe (Twist!)\nJack gives the @GOLDEN_WRENCH to @DAD in the @KITCHEN. Dad fixes the sink and pulls out a mini hacksaw along with @BOX_KEY! Using @BOX_KEY to unlock @GRANDPAS_BOX in @GRANDPAS_ROOM reveals the Twist: @GRANDPA_JOE sabotaged the Ming dish and clogged the sink himself because @GRANDMA plans to evict the family and put Grandpa in a nursing home tonight no matter how clean the kitchen is, all to buy a yacht for her 24-year-old poolboy Raul! From @GRANDPAS_BOX, Jack takes @GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX and the @POOLBOY_PHOTOS.\non_start: |\n  if not tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and not tw.vars.get('kevin_active', False):\n      tw.vars.set('kevin_active', True)\n      tw.npcs.reveal('KEVIN')\n      tw.npcs.move_to_player('KEVIN')\n      tw.npcs.say('KEVIN', 'Hey Jack! Whatcha doing? Got any snacks?')\ngoal_item: GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX\nguard: tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False) and tw.player.has_item('POOLBOY_PHOTOS')\nend: Dad fixes the sink, and Jack unlocks Grandpa's chest to uncover the Poolboy Photos and Grandma's Spice Mix.\n\n[Readable: BOX_KEY] Brass Key with Waterproof Tag\nin: KITCHEN\nhidden: yes\nreveal: script\ntype: KEY\ntext: Tag attached to the key: \"Key to my under-bed chest. I sawed the Ming dish handle and hid the spices, then dropped this key down the drain when my back gave out! - Grandpa Joe\"\n\n[Readable: POOLBOY_PHOTOS] Poolboy Surveillance Photos & Grandpa's Plan\ntype: READABLE\nportable: yes\ntext: Glossy photos of Grandma Evelyn wrestling in a bubbly jacuzzi with her 24-year-old poolboy Raul (who seems to have lost his swim trunks!). Grandpa's note: \"Grandma already signed the papers to sell your house and ship me to Shady Pines tonight! Paperclip these photos to the Marriage Contract from Mom's office (Paragraph 7!) so we can blackmail her at 18:00!\"\n\n[Item: GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX] Grandma's Traditional Spice Mix\ntype: PICKABLE\nStolen from the kitchen by Grandpa during his sabotage spree. Smells of nutmeg, rosemary, and pure authority.\n\n[Sequence: 5] Showdown at the Oven\nBefore 18:00 arrives, Jack must finish all four preparations: (1) If not done yet, unlock @DADS_LOCKER (code 9060) and give @SPORTS_MAGAZINES to @KEVIN so he runs home to \"study for gym class\". (2) Glue @BROKEN_DISH with @SUPER_GLUE into @MING_DISH, thaw @FROZEN_CASSEROLE in the @MICROWAVE, combine @FROZEN_CASSEROLE + @GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX + @MING_DISH via @RECIPE_PREPARE_CASSEROLE into @READY_CASSEROLE, and switch the @OVEN to BAKED while Kevin is gone. (3) Combine @PRENUP_CONTRACT and @POOLBOY_PHOTOS via @RECIPE_BLACKMAIL into @BLACKMAIL_DOSSIER, and either use @BLACKMAIL_DOSSIER in the @KITCHEN or hand it to @GRANDPA_JOE to set the trap for Grandma!\nguard: tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False) and tw.flags.get('CASSEROLE_DONE') and tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and tw.vars.get('grandma_trapped', False)\nend: The sink shines, Kevin is gone, the casserole bakes inside the glued Ming dish, and the Poolboy Blackmail Dossier is ready on the table!\n\n[Switch: MICROWAVE] Microwave\nin: KITCHEN\nstates: OFF=Off, THAWED=Defrosted\ninitial: OFF\ntransition: OFF -> THAWED | item: FROZEN_CASSEROLE | success: Ding! The microwave defrosts the frozen casserole block. Now combine it with Grandma's Spice Mix and the glued Ming Dish!\noutcome: THAWED -> flag: CASSEROLE_THAWED\n\n[Recipe: RECIPE_PREPARE_CASSEROLE] Prepare Casserole in the Ming Dish\ncombine: FROZEN_CASSEROLE + GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX + MING_DISH\ncraft_guard: tw.flags.get('CASSEROLE_THAWED')\nresults: READY_CASSEROLE\non_craft_fail_text: The casserole is still frozen solid! Defrost it in the microwave first.\n\n[Item: READY_CASSEROLE] Spiced Casserole in Ming Dish\ntype: PICKABLE\nThe defrosted casserole seasoned with Grandma's spice mix and resting inside the glued Ming porcelain dish. Ready for the oven!\n\n[Switch: OVEN] Kitchen Oven\nin: KITCHEN\nstates: OFF=Cold, BAKED=Baked & Golden\ninitial: OFF\ntransition: OFF -> BAKED | item: READY_CASSEROLE | guard: tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) | fail: You need the Spiced Casserole in the Ming Dish, and Kevin must be gone from the house or he will raid the oven immediately! | success: The oven heats to 200 degrees. Within minutes, the casserole bakes to golden perfection inside Grandma's Ming dish!\noutcome: BAKED -> flag: CASSEROLE_DONE\non_use: |\n  if tw.switches.is_state('OVEN', 'BAKED'):\n      tw.vars.set('casserole_baked', True)\n      tw.player.remove_item('READY_CASSEROLE')\n      check_victory()\n\n[Recipe: RECIPE_BLACKMAIL] Assemble the Ultimate Grandma Trap\ncombine: PRENUP_CONTRACT + POOLBOY_PHOTOS\nresults: BLACKMAIL_DOSSIER\n\n[Readable: BLACKMAIL_DOSSIER] Poolboy Blackmail Dossier\ntype: READABLE\nportable: yes\ntext: Paragraph 7 of the Miller Marriage Contract (\"100% forfeiture of fortune upon poolside infidelity\") paperclipped directly to high-gloss photos of Grandma Evelyn and her trunkless poolboy Raul in the jacuzzi.\non_use: |\n  if tw.scene.id == 'KITCHEN':\n      tw.vars.set('grandma_trapped', True)\n      tw.player.remove_item('BLACKMAIL_DOSSIER')\n      tw.story.narrate('You place the Poolboy Blackmail Dossier right in the center of the kitchen table on a silver platter. When Grandma inspects the kitchen at 18:00, Paragraph 7 and Poolboy Raul will be the first things she sees!')\n      check_victory()\n  else:\n      tw.story.narrate('Better place this Blackmail Dossier right on the table in the Kitchen, or hand it to Grandpa Joe!')\nThe ultimate legal and photographic leverage against Grandma.",
