      "stamina_change": 0,
      "mana_change": 0,
      "text_log_content": "A folded newspaper crossword, half solved in shaky pencil. In the margin Grandpa Joe scribbled a rhyme:\n\"My son forgets his anniversary date,\nbut the girl on his Mancave wall he recites straight.\nThree numbers she boasts below her pose;\nhis steel locker needs just the top two of those.\nBust first, then waist, and skip the rest:\nthat is how my boy guards his 'sports' chest!\"",
      "text_log_format": "DOCUMENT"
    },
    {
      "id": "KITCHEN_CLOCK",
      "entity_type": "OBJECT",
      "name": "Kitchen Wall Clock",
      "description": "A loudly ticking wall clock above the kitchen door. Grandma arrives at 18:00 sharp. If you are done early, you can sit down and wait for her.",
      "appearance": "round retro kitchen wall clock, white face, black hands, red second hand",
      "current_scene_id": "KITCHEN",
      "spatial_position": "on the wall above the kitchen door",
      "image_url": "assets/2f436b5e_kitchen-clock.webp",
      "item_type": "STATIC",
      "is_in_inventory": false,
      "is_hidden": false,
      "is_portable": false,
      "is_final_state": false,
      "inventory": [],
      "hp_change": 0,
      "stamina_change": 0,
      "mana_change": 0,
      "on_interact_script": "if tw.vars.get('grandma_arrived', False):\n    tw.story.narrate('The clock is ticking on. Grandma is already here.')\nelse:\n    clock_text = str(tw.time.hour) + ':' + str(tw.time.minute).rjust(2, '0')\n    tw.dialog.choose(\n        'The kitchen wall clock shows ' + clock_text + '. Grandma arrives at 18:00 sharp.\\n\\n'\n        'Done early? You can sit down and wait for her right now.\\n\\n'\n        '**Warning:** if the sink is not fixed, Kevin is still around, the casserole is not baking in the glued Ming dish '\n        'or the blackmail trap is not set, Grandma wins and the game is LOST!',\n        ['Wait for Grandma (skip to 18:00)', 'Not yet, keep preparing'],\n        on_choice='on_clock_skip',\n    )"
    },
