  "sequences": [
    {
      "id": "SEQ_1_DISTRACTION",
      "order": 1,
      "title": "Operation Distraction",
      "description": "It is 16:00 on a chaotic afternoon. The clock is ticking toward Grandma Evelyn's arrival, while Mom is locked in her office and Tina is throwing a tantrum upstairs. Jack needs to find a way to get Mom out of her office.",
      "walkthrough": "1. In the Kitchen (KITCHEN), open/inspect the Refrigerator (##FRIDGE) and take the Pink Glitter Energy Drink (##FIZZY_DRINK) and Frozen Casserole Block (##FROZEN_CASSEROLE).\n2. Go to the Living Room (LIVING_ROOM) and read the Fire Department Certificate (##FIRE_CERTIFICATE) on the wall to note the year 2019.\n3. Go upstairs to Tina's Room (TINAS_ROOM) and talk to/interact with Tina (TINA). In the choice dialog, select option 3 ('Here is your Pink Glitter Drink if you scream and lure Mom out of her office!').\n4. Tina stages her drama in the Downstairs Hallway (HALLWAY): Tina, Mom and Jack end up there, and the door to Mom's Office (MOMS_OFFICE) is unlocked. Tina's Room is now empty and Tina's Diary (##TINAS_DIARY) lies on her bed. Go back up to Tina's Room and read ##TINAS_DIARY to learn Mom's desk code is the Fire Certificate year backwards (2019 -> 9102).\n5. Go through the Kitchen into the Downstairs Hallway and enter Mom's Office (MOMS_OFFICE). Pick up the Shattered Ming Casserole Dish (##BROKEN_DISH) and Grandparents' Marriage Contract (##PRENUP_CONTRACT).\n6. Unlock the Locked Desk Drawer (##MOMS_DESK) with code 9102 and take the Pair of AA ##BATTERIES (##BATTERIES) and Crunchy Catnip Treats (##CAT_TREATS).",
      "end_condition": "Jack lures Mom out of her office, collects the broken Ming dish and marriage contract, and unlocks Mom's desk drawer to get the fresh AA ##BATTERIES.",
      "required_item_id": "BATTERIES",
      "exp_reward": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "SEQ_2_MANCAVE",
      "order": 2,
      "title": "Key to the Mancave & Dad's Secret Stash",
      "description": "Grandpa Joe grumbles in his recliner, annoyed by the broken television and the rising tension in the house. Downstairs, mysteries remain behind locked doors.",
      "walkthrough": "1. In the Living Room (LIVING_ROOM), search the Living Room ##COUCH (##COUCH) and take the Empty TV Remote (##EMPTY_REMOTE).\n2. Combine ##EMPTY_REMOTE and ##BATTERIES using the recipe 'Insert ##BATTERIES into Remote' (##RECIPE_REMOTE) to craft the Working TV Remote (##WORKING_REMOTE).\n3. Give ##WORKING_REMOTE to Grandpa Joe (GRANDPA_JOE) in the Living Room. He hands over the Heavy Steel Door Key (##MANCAVE_KEY) and drops a hint about his bed.\n4. (Optional now or in Sequence 5): Talk to Dad in the Kitchen: he lets slip that his locker code is the upper half of the numbers on his Miss Fitness July poster (the first two of the three stats, matching the 4-digit dial). Unlock the hidden steel door from LIVING_ROOM to SECRET_MANCAVE using ##MANCAVE_KEY, read the 'Miss Fitness July' Poster (##FITNESS_POSTER, stats 90 - 60 - 90 -> code 9060), unlock Dad's Locker (##DADS_LOCKER) with 9060, and take the Bundle of 'Sports Magazines' (##SPORTS_MAGAZINES) and Industrial Super Glue (##SUPER_GLUE).",
      "end_condition": "Grandpa Joe turns on the television and slips Jack the key to Dad's Secret Mancave.",
      "required_item_id": "MANCAVE_KEY",
      "exp_reward": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "SEQ_3_PIRANHA",
      "order": 3,
      "title": "Dog, Cat, Piranha!",
      "description": "Dad's secret mancave holds unusual tools and dangerous pets. Getting what Jack needs will take ingenuity and careful handling of the family pets.",
      "walkthrough": "1. Unlock the hidden steel door in the Living Room (LIVING_ROOM) with ##MANCAVE_KEY and enter the Secret Mancave (SECRET_MANCAVE) if not already unlocked.\n2. Make sure you have the Crunchy Catnip Treats (##CAT_TREATS) from Mom's Desk Drawer (##MOMS_DESK, code 9102).\n3. Go to the Backyard (BACKYARD) via the Kitchen patio door and drop ##CAT_TREATS there (right-click the treats in the inventory -> Drop), or use/scatter them. Mr. Whiskers bolts into the yard, Buster chases him through the hedge, and the Half-Gnawed Meaty Bone (##MEATY_BONE) is revealed.\n4. Pick up ##MEATY_BONE, return to the Secret Mancave (SECRET_MANCAVE), and put ##MEATY_BONE into the Piranha Aquarium (##PIRANHA_TANK). The piranhas are distracted and Jack automatically receives the Golden Wrench (##GOLDEN_WRENCH).",
      "end_condition": "The piranhas are busy gnawing on the bone and Jack retrieves Dad's golden wrench from the tank.",
      "required_item_id": "GOLDEN_WRENCH",
      "exp_reward": 150,
      "soft_rules": [
        {
          "id": "LURE_CAT_TO_YARD",
          "condition": "Jack uses or scatters the Crunchy Catnip Treats in the backyard to lure Mr. Whiskers in front of Buster the dog.",
          "script": "lure_cat_action()",
          "guard_expression": "tw.scene.id == 'BACKYARD' and tw.player.has_item('CAT_TREATS') and not tw.vars.get('buster_gone', False)",
          "max_triggers": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "SEQ_4_TWIST",
      "order": 4,
      "title": "The Truth in the Drainpipe (Twist!)",
      "description": "With water threatening to flood the kitchen, the plumbing holds more than just clogged pipes. A secret from Grandpa's past might change everything for the Miller family.",
      "walkthrough": "1. Return to the Kitchen (KITCHEN) and give the Golden Wrench (##GOLDEN_WRENCH) to Dad (DAD).\n2. Dad fixes the sink and hands Jack the Brass Key with Waterproof Tag (##BOX_KEY) that was jammed in the drainpipe alongside a mini hacksaw.\n3. Go to Grandpa's Room (GRANDPAS_ROOM) off the Living Room. Read the Private Detective Invoice (##DETECTIVE_BILL) on the nightstand.\n4. Unlock the Locked Chest Under the Bed (##GRANDPAS_BOX) using ##BOX_KEY and take both the Poolboy Surveillance Photos & Grandpa's Plan (##POOLBOY_PHOTOS) and Grandma's Traditional Spice Mix (##GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX).",
      "end_condition": "Dad fixes the sink, and Jack unlocks Grandpa's chest to uncover the Poolboy Photos and Grandma's Spice Mix.",
      "required_item_id": "GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX",
      "completion_guard_expression": "tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False) and tw.player.has_item('POOLBOY_PHOTOS') and tw.player.has_item('GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX')",
      "exp_reward": 150,
      "on_start_sequence_script": "if not tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and not tw.vars.get('kevin_active', False):\n    tw.vars.set('kevin_active', True)\n    tw.npcs.reveal('KEVIN')\n    tw.npcs.move_to_player('KEVIN')\n    tw.npcs.say('KEVIN', 'Hey Jack! Whatcha doing? Got any snacks?')"
    },
    {
      "id": "SEQ_5_SHOWDOWN",
      "order": 5,
      "title": "Showdown at the ##OVEN",
      "description": "The final minutes before 18:00 tick away. The dining table awaits dinner, the kitchen smells of impending doom, and Grandma's footsteps will soon echo at the front door.",
      "walkthrough": "1. In the Secret Mancave (SECRET_MANCAVE), read the 'Miss Fitness July' Poster (##FITNESS_POSTER, stats 90 - 60 - 90) and unlock Dad's 'Strictly Athletics' Locker (##DADS_LOCKER) using code 9060 (the upper half of the stats, as hinted by Dad and by Grandpa's rhyme on the crossword page hidden in his slippers, ##GRANDPAS_CROSSWORD). Take the Bundle of 'Sports Magazines' (##SPORTS_MAGAZINES) and Industrial Super Glue (##SUPER_GLUE).\n2. Give ##SPORTS_MAGAZINES to Kevin (KEVIN) so he rushes home to 'study for gym class'.\n3. Combine the Shattered Ming Casserole Dish (##BROKEN_DISH) and Industrial Super Glue (##SUPER_GLUE) via ##RECIPE_GLUE_DISH into the Glued Ming Casserole Dish (##MING_DISH).\n4. In the Kitchen (KITCHEN), make sure you have the Frozen Casserole Block (##FROZEN_CASSEROLE) from the ##FRIDGE, then put it into the ##MICROWAVE (##MICROWAVE) and switch it from OFF to THAWED to defrost it into the Thawed Casserole (##THAWED_CASSEROLE).\n5. Combine ##THAWED_CASSEROLE, ##GRANDMAS_SPICE_MIX, and ##MING_DISH via ##RECIPE_PREPARE_CASSEROLE into the Spiced Casserole in Ming Dish (##READY_CASSEROLE).\n6. Switch the Kitchen ##OVEN (##OVEN) from OFF to BAKED (requires ##READY_CASSEROLE and Kevin gone).\n7. Combine Grandparents' Marriage Contract (##PRENUP_CONTRACT) and Poolboy Surveillance Photos (##POOLBOY_PHOTOS) via ##RECIPE_BLACKMAIL into the Poolboy Blackmail Dossier (##BLACKMAIL_DOSSIER).\n8. Use/interact with ##BLACKMAIL_DOSSIER in the Kitchen (or give it to Grandpa Joe in the Living Room) to set the trap.\n9. Wait for Grandma at 18:00, or use the Kitchen Wall Clock (##KITCHEN_CLOCK) to skip ahead. When she arrives, the whole family gathers in the Kitchen for the showdown and you win!",
      "end_condition": "The sink shines, Kevin is gone, the casserole bakes inside the glued Ming dish, and the Poolboy Blackmail Dossier is ready on the table!",
      "guard_expression": "tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False) and tw.flags.get('CASSEROLE_DONE') and tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and tw.vars.get('grandma_trapped', False)",
      "completion_guard_expression": "tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False) and tw.flags.get('CASSEROLE_DONE') and tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and tw.vars.get('grandma_trapped', False)",
      "exp_reward": 250
    }
  ],
  "scripts": [
    {
      "id": "TIMELINE_1600_INTRO",
      "name": "16:00 Chaos Start",
      "trigger": "on_init",
      "target_id": null,
      "target": null,
      "code": "tw.story.narrate('It is 16:00 sharp! In exactly two hours, tyrannical Grandma arrives for dinner inspection. Mom locks herself inside her home office in tears. Tina slams her bedroom door upstairs. Dad is kneeling under the flooded kitchen sink, cursing because he cannot find his golden wrench, while Grandpa Joe grumbles in front of the dead TV. Everything is up to you, Jack!')",
      "description": "Initializes the 16:00 opening narration."
    },
    {
      "id": "TIMELINE_1630_KEVIN",
      "name": "16:30 Kevin Appears",
      "trigger": "on_time_reached",
      "target_id": "30",
      "target": "30",
      "code": "if not tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and not tw.vars.get('kevin_active', False):\n    tw.vars.set('kevin_active', True)\n    tw.npcs.reveal('KEVIN')\n    tw.npcs.move_to_player('KEVIN')\n    tw.npcs.say('KEVIN', 'Hey Jack! Do I smell dinner? Got five bucks or something to eat?')\n    tw.story.narrate('16:30 sharp: Annoying neighbor Kevin suddenly stands right next to you, uninvited!')",
      "description": "Spawns neighbor Kevin at 16:30 (30 minutes elapsed)."
    },
    {
      "id": "TIMELINE_1700_WARNING",
      "name": "17:00 One Hour Left",
      "trigger": "on_time_reached",
      "target_id": "60",
      "target": "60",
      "code": "tw.story.narrate('The wall clock chimes 17:00! Only one hour left until Grandma arrives, and Dad is still sweating buckets under the sink!')",
      "description": "One hour warning at 17:00."
    },
    {
      "id": "TIMELINE_1745_PANIC",
      "name": "17:45 Fifteen Minutes Left",
      "trigger": "on_time_reached",
      "target_id": "105",
      "target": "105",
      "code": "tw.story.narrate('It is 17:45! Grandma\\'s taxi just turned onto your street! Fifteen minutes left, hurry up!')",
      "description": "Fifteen minutes left warning at 17:45."
    },
    {
      "id": "KEVIN_STALKER",
      "name": "Kevin Follows Jack Everywhere and Wastes Time",
      "trigger": "on_enter_scene",
      "target": null,
      "code": "if tw.vars.get('kevin_active', False) and not tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False):\n    # Kevin sticks to Jack from scene to scene; the time-wasting chatter stays random.\n    tw.npcs.move_to_player('KEVIN', \"right on Jack's heels\")\n    if tw.dice.d6() >= 3:\n        tw.time.advance(3)\n        tw.npcs.say_directed('KEVIN', 'pesters Jack with pointless questions about food, pocket money, or video games, wasting 3 precious minutes')\n",
      "priority": 100,
      "is_active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "TIMELINE_1800_GRANDMA",
      "name": "18:00 Grandma Arrives in the Kitchen",
      "trigger": "on_time_reached",
      "target": "120",
      "code": "grandma_arrives()\n",
      "priority": 100,
      "is_active": true
    }
  ],
  "init_script": "tw.time.set_minutes_per_tick(3)\ntw.time.allow_gm_time(False)\ntw.vars.set('kevin_active', False)\ntw.vars.set('kevin_gone', False)\ntw.vars.set('sink_fixed', False)\ntw.vars.set('casserole_baked', False)\ntw.vars.set('grandma_trapped', False)\ntw.vars.set('buster_gone', False)\ndef all_prepared():\n    return tw.vars.get('sink_fixed', False) and tw.flags.get('CASSEROLE_DONE') and tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False) and tw.vars.get('grandma_trapped', False)\ndef check_victory():\n    # The win happens in the showdown when Grandma arrives; here Jack only learns he is ready.\n    if not all_prepared() or tw.vars.get('ready_announced', False) or tw.vars.get('grandma_arrived', False):\n        return\n    tw.vars.set('ready_announced', True)\n    tw.story.narrate('Everything is ready: the sink shines, Kevin is gone, the casserole bakes in the glued Ming dish and the Poolboy Blackmail Dossier is in place. Now Grandma can come! If you do not want to wait until 18:00, check the wall clock in the kitchen.')\ndef lure_cat_action():\n    if tw.vars.get('buster_gone', False):\n        return\n    tw.vars.set('buster_gone', True)\n    # The treats may still be carried (soft rule) or already lie in the backyard (dropped).\n    tw.objects.destroy('CAT_TREATS')\n    tw.npcs.move('CAT_WHISKERS', 'BACKYARD')\n    tw.npcs.hide('CAT_WHISKERS')\n    tw.npcs.hide('DOG_BUSTER')\n    tw.objects.reveal('MEATY_BONE')\n    tw.story.narrate('Drawn by the irresistible scent of crunchy catnip, Mr. Whiskers bolts into the backyard! Buster the bulldog loses his mind, abandons his meaty bone, and chases the cat barking wildly through the garden hedge!')\ndef on_tina_dialog(answ):\n    if answ == 0:\n        tw.player.damage(2)\n        tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'Get out of my room, you little dork!')\n        tw.story.narrate('Tina hurls a heavy decorative pillow right at your face (-2 HP).')\n        return\n    if answ == 1:\n        tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'Nice try! Mom locked herself in her office until five.')\n        return\n    if answ == 2:\n        start_tina_drama()\n\n\ndef start_tina_drama():\n    # Tina drinks the can, wherever it is (Jack's hands or already hers after a handover).\n    tw.objects.destroy('FIZZY_DRINK')\n    tw.vars.set('tina_bribed', True)\n    tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'OMG, Pink Glitter Zero! Step back and watch a master of teenage drama at work...')\n\n    # Act 1: Tina stages the drama in the hallway; Jack follows her down. Mom is still inside.\n    tw.npcs.move('TINA', 'HALLWAY', \"wailing in front of Mom's office door, clutching a smoking hair straightener\")\n    tw.scene.teleport('HALLWAY')\n    if tw.vars.get('kevin_active', False) and not tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False):\n        tw.npcs.move_to_player('KEVIN', 'gawking at the drama with his mouth wide open')\n    tw.story.narrate(\"Tina storms down the stairs, drops to her knees in front of Mom's locked office door and takes a deep breath. You follow her into the hallway just in time.\")\n    tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'MOOOOM! HELP! MY HAIR STRAIGHTENER EXPLODED AND MY EYEBROWS ARE GONE!')\n\n    # Act 2 follows right away: the client continues the scene, the narration tells the\n    # rattling key, and only then Mom bursts out (callback), so she appears after the scream.\n    tw.story.direct(\n        \"Tina keeps wailing in front of Mom's locked office door. Inside the office a chair scrapes \"\n        \"over the floor and a key starts rattling in the lock. Mom has NOT come out yet: end the \"\n        \"narration right before the door opens.\",\n        after='mom_bursts_out'\n    )\n\n\ndef mom_bursts_out():\n    tw.exits.unlock('HALLWAY', 'MOMS_OFFICE')\n    tw.npcs.move('MOM', 'HALLWAY', \"kneeling next to Tina and inspecting her eyebrows in total panic\")\n    tw.objects.reveal('TINAS_DIARY')\n    if tw.scene.id == 'HALLWAY':\n        tw.story.narrate(\"The office door flies open and Mom rushes out in total panic, leaving the door wide open behind her.\")\n        tw.npcs.say('MOM', 'Tina?! Oh my God, let me see! Where does it hurt, sweetheart?!')\n    else:\n        tw.story.narrate(\"From the hallway you hear Mom's office door bang open, and her panicked voice joins Tina's wailing.\")\n    if tw.scene.id == 'TINAS_ROOM':\n        tw.story.narrate(\"With Tina gone, you spot her secret diary lying on the unmade bed.\")\n    else:\n        tw.story.narrate(\"Upstairs, Tina's bedroom now stands empty - and in her hurry she left her secret diary lying on the bed.\")\n\n\ndef on_tina_drink_deal(answ):\n    if answ == 0:\n        start_tina_drama()\n        return\n    # No deal named: Tina is suspicious and hands the can back, so the puzzle stays solvable.\n    tw.npcs.give_to_player('TINA', 'FIZZY_DRINK')\n    tw.npcs.say('TINA', 'A gift? From you? Nobody gives me stuff for free. Come back when you know what you want, dork.')\n\ndef grandma_arrives():\n    # Shared by the 18:00 time event and the kitchen clock; runs only once.\n    if tw.vars.get('grandma_arrived', False):\n        return\n    tw.vars.set('grandma_arrived', True)\n    # The verdict is fixed at the moment she walks in; the game ends after her reaction.\n    tw.vars.set('grandma_ready', bool(all_prepared()))\n\n    # Showdown: Jack and the whole household gather in the kitchen.\n    tw.scene.teleport('KITCHEN')\n    showdown_npcs = [\n        ('DAD', 'standing proudly next to the gleaming, dry kitchen sink'),\n        ('MOM', 'nervously smoothing her apron by the dining table'),\n        ('TINA', 'leaning against the fridge, filming everything on her phone'),\n        ('GRANDPA_JOE', 'sitting at the head of the dining table with a sly grin'),\n    ]\n    for npc_id, position in showdown_npcs:\n        tw.npcs.move(npc_id, 'KITCHEN', position)\n    if tw.vars.get('kevin_active', False) and not tw.vars.get('kevin_gone', False):\n        tw.npcs.move('KEVIN', 'KITCHEN', 'munching a stolen bread roll in the corner')\n    tw.npcs.move('GRANDMA', 'KITCHEN', 'standing in the kitchen doorway in her fur coat, eviction papers in hand')\n    tw.npcs.reveal('GRANDMA')\n    tw.story.narrate('DING-DONG! 18:00 sharp. The whole family hurries into the kitchen as the front door swings open and the click of expensive heels echoes through the hallway. Grandma Evelyn sweeps in, eviction papers in her gloved hand, and lets her icy gaze wander over the kitchen...')\n\n    opened = tw.dialog.choose(\n        'Grandma Evelyn is standing in the kitchen. All eyes are on you, Jack.',\n        ['Face Grandma'],\n        on_choice='on_grandma_showdown',\n        speaker='Grandma',\n    )\n    if not opened:\n        start_showdown()\n\ndef on_grandma_showdown(answ):\n    start_showdown()\n\ndef start_showdown():\n    # Grandma reacts in the next narration; only then grandma_verdict ends the game.\n    if tw.vars.get('grandma_ready', False):\n        tw.npcs.say_directed(\n            'GRANDMA',\n            'inspects the spotless sink and her Ming dish in the oven, about to find something to complain about, '\n            'then spots the Poolboy Blackmail Dossier on the table: photos of her and Poolboy Raul clipped to Paragraph 7 '\n            'of her Marriage Contract. She is utterly shocked and stammers in disbelief',\n            after='grandma_verdict',\n        )\n    else:\n        tw.npcs.say_directed(\n            'GRANDMA',\n            'looks around the kitchen, surprised and delighted at how badly the Millers failed, and points out with '\n            'cruel glee everything that is not ready for her inspection',\n            after='grandma_verdict',\n        )\n\ndef grandma_verdict():\n    if tw.vars.get('grandma_ready', False):\n        tw.vars.set('grandma_showdown_won', True)\n        tw.npcs.say('GRANDMA', 'Fine! FINE! Keep the house, and Joe can stay here forever! Just... burn those photos!')\n        tw.game.win('18:00 sharp: Grandma is completely checkmated by the spotless kitchen AND the Poolboy Blackmail Dossier! She tears up the eviction notice, signs the house over to Dad and flees into the night.')\n    else:\n        tw.vars.set('grandma_failed', True)\n        tw.npcs.say('GRANDMA', 'Just as I expected! An absolute pigsty, and no leverage to stop me! Pack your bags, Millers, I am selling this house and shipping Joe to Shady Pines tonight!')\n        tw.game.game_over('18:00 sharp: Grandma stands in the kitchen with the eviction papers. You are grounded until 2035!')\n\ndef on_clock_skip(answ):\n    if answ != 0:\n        tw.story.narrate('You leave the clock alone. Every minute counts, so back to work!')\n        return\n    # Jump straight to Grandma's arrival; time events would only fire after the next narration.\n    if tw.time.now < 120:\n        tw.time.set(120)\n    tw.story.narrate('You flop down at the kitchen table and stare at the wall clock until its hands finally crawl to 18:00...')\n    grandma_arrives()"
}